From 817fd1241eaf9b37913e559a23d28ece56798e6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:16:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: a TRef member read out of a tree resolves through
 its TProcessID

roottest/root/io/tree/test-r now prints the names its reference names, and
the six tests of that family that died reading a TRef record now run.

- references: TRef::Streamer resolves fPID through gFile as it reads, since a
  record handed to the reader carries only the index of the file's process;
  filed_object files an object read that a reference may point at, keyed by
  the number in its identifier, in the file's process its top byte indexes.
- trees: a reference that finds no object asks the tree being read for the
  entry's collections (TRefTable keeps them alive - a process table holds its
  objects weakly), once per entry, since a process numbers from the start in
  each entry. A clone fills a split collection from the objects its source
  tree was given rather than from the values last read, which is what numbers
  them; and a collection written into a tree now writes the file's
  ProcessID records, which only the object-level writer did before.
- printing: Show prints a member of one string per object as text and a
  member of whole objects as the pointer it is, instead of int() of a name.

Still DIFF, not PASS: seven tests of the family differ in Show's output
formatting (leaf names, line breaks) which is untouched here.
